      "message": "fix(import): mesh rational B-spline thread strips closed and at full fidelity\n\nA thread flank or root exported as one rational strip (degree 1 across,\ndegree 2 along in 36-degree arcs, ~14 turns) meshed into ~2 M facets with\na 0.5-3 mm hole. Three causes, fixed in the importer's face wrapper:\n\n- step_division: split a parameter direction only where it is curved\n  (truck's division split both directions of every failing cell, so a\n  strip curved along v got 2^sweeps intervals across u). A division still\n  splitting after 64 sweeps (a jump) exhausts the face's evaluation\n  budget and is refused by name as before.\n- step_stretch: stretch the faster parameter of a B-spline/NURBS face by\n  its speed ratio (> 4:1), so truck's Delaunay trimming triangulation\n  works in a plane with the face's proportions.\n- step_nearest: an answer from truck's parameter search that lies off the\n  surface or outside the knot domain is searched again from a sample grid\n  with points in every knot span; the nearest answer inside the domain\n  wins when it is on the surface or nearer.\n\n10208.STEP: 6.1 M facets / 31-72 s -> 13,662 facets / 1.9 s at 0.005 mm;\n32050.STEP: 5.0 M / 62-130 s -> 8,128 / 1.7 s; both close under #1576's\nclosed-shell check.\n\nFixes #1602\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
